WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.249
Responsible communication protects accuracy and reduces harm.

00:00:03.249 --> 00:00:04.148
Avoid overclaiming.

00:00:04.148 --> 00:00:08.196
State the claim examined, evidence reviewed, conclusion reached, confidence,

00:00:08.196 --> 00:00:09.546
and important limitations.

00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:13.594
Separate technical observations from judgments about authenticity or intent.

00:00:13.594 --> 00:00:14.943
Use labels precisely.

00:00:14.943 --> 00:00:17.642
Unverified means available evidence is insufficient.

00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:20.791
Manipulated means supported alterations changed the media.

00:00:20.791 --> 00:00:23.939
Synthetic means generation is supported by evidence.

00:00:23.939 --> 00:00:30.686
Miscontextualized means genuine or partly genuine media is paired with a false or misleading context.

00:00:30.686 --> 00:00:32.935
These labels are not interchangeable.

00:00:32.935 --> 00:00:36.533
A clip can be unverified without being fake,

00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:39.682
and manipulated media can contain genuine events.

00:00:39.682 --> 00:00:41.931
Disinformation additionally implies deceptive intent,

00:00:41.931 --> 00:00:45.080
which may require evidence beyond the file.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:48.228
Use calibrated confidence language and explain why.

00:00:48.228 --> 00:00:51.827
High confidence should reflect strong provenance, independent corroboration,

00:00:51.827 --> 00:00:54.975
consistent technical findings, and limited plausible alternatives.

00:00:54.975 --> 00:00:58.573
A detector score alone does not justify certainty.

00:00:58.573 --> 00:01:03.071
Sensitive media may involve victims, private individuals, sexual content, violence,

00:01:03.071 --> 00:01:04.421
or reputational accusations.

00:01:04.421 --> 00:01:09.369
Limit distribution, avoid unnecessary reproduction, protect personal details, and follow legal,

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.618
safeguarding, and organizational reporting procedures.

00:01:11.618 --> 00:01:13.867
Support truth without amplifying harm.

00:01:13.867 --> 00:01:18.814
Lead with verified context rather than sensational repetition, correct errors promptly,

00:01:18.814 --> 00:01:21.513
and preserve evidence for accountable review.

00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:28.260
The best report helps the audience make a proportionate decision while remaining honest about uncertainty.
